### Backend objects the UI must consume (not recompute)

```
PipelineResult
  ├── evidence_package: EvidencePackage
  │     ├── detection: {actual_value, delta_absolute, delta_relative, test_statistic, material}
  │     ├── decomposition: {drivers[], residual_pct, dominant_driver, no_dominant_contributor}
  │     ├── segmentation: {ranked_stores[], excluded_stores[]}
  │     ├── baseline: {baseline_mean, baseline_std, window_size_used}
  │     ├── day_month_links: []
  │     └── data_state, evaluated_on_stale_input, terminal_outcome
  ├── hypothesis_package: HypothesisPackage
  │     ├── hypotheses[]: {driver_type, confidence_score, confidence_band, confidence_components, status}
  │     └── decision: {outcome, leading_hypothesis_id, caveat_text, memory_context}
  ├── decision_package: DecisionPackage
  │     ├── actions[]: ActionItem {driver, controllable_lever, action, expected_impact, owner, confidence, monitoring_plan}
  │     ├── narrative_zone_business_head
  │     └── narrative_dark_store_ops_manager
  ├── memory_result: {matched, match_scope, confirmed_precedent_count, demo_fixture_involved}
  └── telemetry_summary: {total_latency_ms, total_llm_calls, total_tokens, total_cost_usd}
```

### What the current UI does (gaps to fix)
- Flat tab structure — no coherent navigation
- No application shell (header with context, persona switcher)
- No clear progressive disclosure (What changed? → Why? → What to do?)
- No dedicated Investigation workspace
- No Past Decisions page
- No dedicated Memory as organizational learning page
- No Data Health page
- No Access & Entitlements page
- Evidence is text-only — no traceability structure
- Confidence shown as number only — not explained
- No abstention scenario presented as a strength

